00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:27.158
One for each of the Stark children.

00:01:27.158 --> 00:01:30.272
The direwolf is the sigil of your house.

00:01:30.272 --> 00:01:32.522
We were meant to have them.

00:01:33.757 --> 00:01:35.755
- You will train them yourselves.

00:01:35.755 --> 00:01:38.065
You'll feed them yourselves.

00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:41.952
And if they die, you'll
bury them yourselves.

00:01:41.952 --> 00:01:44.950
- When I did return to
books, I said to myself,

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.171
okay, I've had many things optioned.

00:01:48.171 --> 00:01:50.121
They never make them.

00:01:50.121 --> 00:01:51.960
I've done pilots and TV
shows, tried to keep them

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.688
within budget and produce
able, and they never make that.

00:01:54.688 --> 00:01:57.037
I'm tired of playing that game.

00:01:57.037 --> 00:01:59.156
I'm going to, you know I
have a big imagination,

00:01:59.156 --> 00:02:00.518
I have an epic story I want to tell,

00:02:00.518 --> 00:02:02.041
I'm going to make it as
big as my imagination.

00:02:02.041 --> 00:02:05.176
I'm going to have all the
castles and battles I want.

00:02:05.176 --> 00:02:07.076
I'm going to have hundreds of characters

00:02:07.076 --> 00:02:08.516
because the real world
is complex and I want

00:02:08.516 --> 00:02:10.909
my fictional world to be complex too,

00:02:10.909 --> 00:02:12.991
not a kind of simplified thing.

00:02:12.991 --> 00:02:14.416
I want to have giant battles.

00:02:14.416 --> 00:02:16.437
I want to have incredible castles

00:02:16.437 --> 00:02:18.597
that each one is distinct from the other

00:02:18.597 --> 00:02:20.619
that people will remember for all time.

00:02:20.619 --> 00:02:22.649
I want to have dragons and direwolves

00:02:22.649 --> 00:02:26.654
and mammoths and a wall of
ice that's 700 feet tall.

00:02:26.654 --> 00:02:28.890
I want something huge and epic

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:31.973
that can stand up there with Tolkien.

00:02:32.996 --> 00:02:34.692
- A funny thing happens
when you start setting

00:02:34.692 --> 00:02:37.116
bigger goals for yourself
or you start imagining

00:02:37.116 --> 00:02:40.175
a bigger future potential for yourself.

00:02:40.175 --> 00:02:42.658
You start to accomplish bigger things.

00:02:42.658 --> 00:02:45.908
Most people have really, really
small goals for themselves

00:02:45.908 --> 00:02:48.543
and when they hit it, they're
happy they hit their goal,

00:02:48.543 --> 00:02:50.230
and then they set
another really small goal

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.824
for themselves, and they
continue to live small.

00:02:52.824 --> 00:02:55.113
And they continue to play small because

00:02:55.113 --> 00:02:56.541
their thinking is small.

00:02:56.541 --> 00:02:58.848
Because their ambitions are small.

00:02:58.848 --> 00:03:00.513
And as long as you're happy, that's great,

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:03.703
that's fine, but I think if
you have the ability to do more

00:03:03.703 --> 00:03:06.401
then you have the responsibility
to do more as well.

00:03:06.401 --> 00:03:07.720
And I encourage all of you to think,

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.941
how can I do something bigger?

00:03:08.941 --> 00:03:11.453
How can I have a bigger goal for myself?

00:03:11.453 --> 00:03:14.713
How can I stretch myself
to do a little bit more

00:03:14.713 --> 00:03:16.599
than what is comfortable for me?

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:17.907
If I look at my overall
goal, I want to help

00:03:17.907 --> 00:03:19.310
a billion entrepreneurs.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.860
I want to have a billion
entrepreneurs in my lifetime,

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.541
like how does that happen?

00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:25.080
A lot of people look at
that goal and they say

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:26.487
that's impossible, that's
never going to happen.

00:03:26.487 --> 00:03:28.350
A lot of people say well
how do you track it?

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.464
Are there even a billion entrepreneurs

00:03:29.464 --> 00:03:30.718
out there in the world?

00:03:30.718 --> 00:03:33.281
And the people who think
like that, the people

00:03:33.281 --> 00:03:35.970
who come from that world of scarcity.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:37.377
They think small.

00:03:37.377 --> 00:03:39.976
They are not out doing amazing things.

00:03:39.976 --> 00:03:41.688
You need to avoid those people.

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.090
Those people are like a disease.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:46.299
Their small thinking
can be a disease to you.

00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:48.800
Their doubt, their negativity,
their small thinking

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.533
can seep into you to shrink yourself down.

00:03:52.533 --> 00:03:54.309
You want to go off and
do this amazing thing,

00:03:54.309 --> 00:03:56.092
but then all the people
around you are negative,

00:03:56.092 --> 00:03:58.049
and what they're doing is pulling on you,

00:03:58.049 --> 00:04:00.614
and they pull you right
back down to where you were.

00:04:00.614 --> 00:04:01.920
Because you don't want
to be judged by them,

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.357
because you don't want to disappoint them,

00:04:03.357 --> 00:04:05.786
because you don't want
to fail in front of them.

00:04:05.786 --> 00:04:08.388
That's toxic, and you may
not be able to totally

00:04:08.388 --> 00:04:09.988
eliminate those people from your life,

00:04:09.988 --> 00:04:11.423
like maybe that's your mom.

00:04:11.423 --> 00:04:12.880
And maybe there's a lot of
great things about your mom,

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:14.952
but this piece you don't like,

00:04:14.952 --> 00:04:17.223
so you may not be able
to completely brush aside

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:19.591
these people, but you can supplement

00:04:19.591 --> 00:04:21.530
with a lot of greatness.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.994
You can supplement with
videos and people and ideas

00:04:23.994 --> 00:04:26.648
and resources and thoughts and books

00:04:26.648 --> 00:04:29.655
that make you want to play a bigger game.

00:04:29.655 --> 00:04:32.273
If you hung around
George R.R. Martin more,

00:04:32.273 --> 00:04:34.305
you would aim higher, you would have

00:04:34.305 --> 00:04:35.926
bigger goals for yourself.

00:04:35.926 --> 00:04:37.079
It's why I have this channel.

00:04:37.079 --> 00:04:39.788
That's why I have the mentor
me series and the top 10,

00:04:39.788 --> 00:04:41.045
to hang around these people more,

00:04:41.045 --> 00:04:42.808
people you might never
ever meet in your life.

00:04:42.808 --> 00:04:44.307
Some people have passed
on, some people you

00:04:44.307 --> 00:04:48.238
may never get access to, to
get more of their wisdom,

00:04:48.238 --> 00:04:50.302
their thought process, their mindset,

00:04:50.302 --> 00:04:53.161
because if you hang around
people and are consuming

00:04:53.161 --> 00:04:57.061
content of people who are thinking big,

00:04:57.061 --> 00:04:59.268
you are going to want to think big too.

00:04:59.268 --> 00:05:01.160
And it doesn't mean
you need to read a book

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:04.168
on seven way to think big,
that's one way to do it,

00:05:04.168 --> 00:05:06.188
you knoW the how-to step-by-step approach,

00:05:06.188 --> 00:05:08.045
but just by osmosis,
just by hanging around

00:05:08.045 --> 00:05:10.711
and watching people thinking
big, it'll naturally

00:05:10.711 --> 00:05:14.362
seep into you to want to think
bigger and do more as well.

00:05:14.362 --> 00:05:16.275
When I first started work with Lily,

00:05:16.275 --> 00:05:18.319
and decided to take her on and mentor her

00:05:18.319 --> 00:05:20.693
and build her up to be an entrepreneur,

00:05:20.693 --> 00:05:23.026
her big goal was to do a Tedx talk.

00:05:23.026 --> 00:05:24.240
That's what she wanted to do,

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:25.443
like I want to be a Ted ex speaker.

00:05:25.443 --> 00:05:26.422
I need to, my big goal as a speaker

00:05:26.422 --> 00:05:28.000
is I want to get on Tedx.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.449
Tedx is nothing, Tedx is small.

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:32.200
I mean I have respect
for Ted and everything

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.435
they're doing at Tedx conferences,

00:05:34.435 --> 00:05:36.916
but you're so much more
talented than that.

00:05:36.916 --> 00:05:40.179
You have so much more of a
ceiling than just doing a Tedx.

00:05:40.179 --> 00:05:42.817
And she saw that as being a one year goal,

00:05:42.817 --> 00:05:45.159
or two year goal, or
something off in the future.

00:05:45.159 --> 00:05:47.939
Like no we're going to, you're
going to apply right now.

00:05:47.939 --> 00:05:50.550
You are going to start researching Ted,

00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:53.389
you're going to look at all
the ones that are coming up,

00:05:53.389 --> 00:05:55.386
and you're going to
start applying right now.

00:05:55.386 --> 00:05:57.534
And she got her first
one, and she's leaving

00:05:57.534 --> 00:06:00.835
to go do her first Tedx
talk, and she's applying

00:06:00.835 --> 00:06:03.585
some more, and the new goal
that we created together

00:06:03.585 --> 00:06:07.123
is for her to be the most
prolific Tedx talk speaker ever.

00:06:07.123 --> 00:06:10.367
I don't know how many people
have done multiple Tedx talks,

00:06:10.367 --> 00:06:12.111
have done like three or
four, I don't know what

00:06:12.111 --> 00:06:14.667
the highest is, but the goal
is for her to be the highest,

00:06:14.667 --> 00:06:17.224
to have the highest, the
most number of Tedx talks.

00:06:17.224 --> 00:06:19.853
And so taking that goal of
something that's way down

00:06:19.853 --> 00:06:22.761
in the future and bringing it to today,

00:06:22.761 --> 00:06:25.646
taking that big thing that
you think is impossible

00:06:25.646 --> 00:06:28.605
that maybe one day will happen,

00:06:28.605 --> 00:06:30.883
and making it happen sooner.

00:06:30.883 --> 00:06:33.622
Taking the recent goal that
you had and you just hit,

00:06:33.622 --> 00:06:36.702
and that was a safe, easy,
comfortable goal to hit,

00:06:36.702 --> 00:06:38.027
and make it bigger.

00:06:38.027 --> 00:06:40.037
It's like I don't know how
I'm going to get there,

00:06:40.037 --> 00:06:41.969
but I'm going to try to figure it out.

00:06:41.969 --> 00:06:45.097
Like when you set yourself
a target and a goal,

00:06:45.097 --> 00:06:47.065
you're much more likely to have your brain

00:06:47.065 --> 00:06:48.152
then try to figure out okay,

00:06:48.152 --> 00:06:50.050
how am I going to accomplish it?

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.002
When I set my goal this
year to hit a million

00:06:52.002 --> 00:06:54.119
YouTube subscribers by
the end of the year,

00:06:54.119 --> 00:06:55.966
I had nothing to justify that.

00:06:55.966 --> 00:06:58.199
You know my growth rate wasn't on track,

00:06:58.199 --> 00:07:01.505
I would be way short,
but having that as a goal

00:07:01.505 --> 00:07:04.494
then tweaks my mind,
okay how do we do that.

00:07:04.494 --> 00:07:07.130
How do we up our production quality?

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.174
How do we bring on better videos?

00:07:08.174 --> 00:07:10.457
How do we give more value
to you guys watching

00:07:10.457 --> 00:07:12.535
so that you want to watch
more, you want to share more,

00:07:12.535 --> 00:07:14.096
you want to tell your friends about it.

00:07:14.096 --> 00:07:16.998
You want to, more importantly,
go out and do something

00:07:16.998 --> 00:07:18.672
in your life in your business as a result

00:07:18.672 --> 00:07:21.434
of watching the videos
and now we're on track.

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:25.253
We're on track for late
December, but it's on track.

00:07:25.253 --> 00:07:27.668
And hopefully we continue
to climb and grow

00:07:27.668 --> 00:07:29.863
and we hit it, and what seemed
like a crazy stretch goal

00:07:29.863 --> 00:07:33.731
at the beginning of the
year, is now achievable.

00:07:33.731 --> 00:07:35.597
And so I want the same thing for you.

00:07:35.597 --> 00:07:38.109
Take whatever goal you have
that you've been hitting

00:07:38.109 --> 00:07:41.379
consistently and stretch
it more, aim bigger,

00:07:41.379 --> 00:07:42.812
believe in yourself more.

00:07:42.812 --> 00:07:44.487
Stop listening to the naysayers

00:07:44.487 --> 00:07:45.541
and the doubters and the haters

00:07:45.541 --> 00:07:47.775
and the small thinking people around you.

00:07:47.775 --> 00:07:49.645
It's not that they're evil or bad,

00:07:49.645 --> 00:07:50.948
we're not you know judging them,

00:07:50.948 --> 00:07:53.853
just stop listening to them.

00:07:53.853 --> 00:07:55.173
Believe in yourself more,

00:07:55.173 --> 00:07:57.202
surround yourself with the
resources that build you up

00:07:57.202 --> 00:07:58.536
and make you feel unstoppable

00:07:58.536 --> 00:08:00.167
and give you boldness and courage,

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:02.172
and implement that into your daily routine

00:08:02.172 --> 00:08:04.584
so that you wake up every
day and do the thing

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:06.032
that makes you feel bold and courageous.

00:08:06.032 --> 00:08:07.878
If you did that every day for a year,

00:08:07.878 --> 00:08:09.722
just imagine where you would be compared

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:11.265
to where you are right now.

00:08:11.265 --> 00:08:12.840
Aim higher.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.174
And so the question of the day today is,

00:08:14.174 --> 00:08:17.140
I'm curious, what is your big goal?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:18.496
What's the big thing that
you're trying to accomplish?

00:08:18.496 --> 00:08:20.167
What's the big impact that
you're trying to make?

00:08:20.167 --> 00:08:21.540
I'd love to hear from you.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:22.982
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:08:22.982 --> 00:08:24.876
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Rich.

00:08:24.876 --> 00:08:27.261
Rich thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:08:27.261 --> 00:08:29.513
Your One Word, it really
means a lot to me,

00:08:29.513 --> 00:08:31.927
your support, and I hope
you enjoyed the read.

00:08:31.927 --> 00:08:33.282
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:08:33.282 --> 00:08:34.530
I believe in you.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:35.815
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:39.015
and whatever your one word is, much love,

00:08:39.015 --> 00:08:40.720
and I'll see you guys
again tomorrow morning

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.792
for another shot of enspresso.

00:08:43.792 --> 00:08:46.097
♫ I wake up every morning

00:08:46.097 --> 00:08:49.075
♫ Enspresso keep me going

00:08:49.075 --> 00:08:51.742
♫ Every morning

00:08:53.015 --> 00:08:56.069
- If you can figure your
life so that what you are

00:08:56.069 --> 00:09:00.236
genuinely doing is aiming at
the highest possible good,

00:09:01.567 --> 00:09:04.900
then the things that you need to survive

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.391
and to thrive on a day to day basis,

00:09:09.391 --> 00:09:12.706
will deliver themselves to you.

00:09:12.706 --> 00:09:16.161
That's a hypothesis, and it's
not some simple hypothesis,

00:09:16.161 --> 00:09:17.959
right, because what it basically says is,

00:09:17.959 --> 00:09:19.833
if you dare to do the most difficult thing

00:09:19.833 --> 00:09:23.373
that you conceptualize, your
life will work out better

00:09:23.373 --> 00:09:26.054
than it will if you do anything else.

00:09:26.054 --> 00:09:27.754
Well how are you going to
find out if that's true?

00:09:27.754 --> 00:09:29.890
Well it's a character
guardian leap of faith.

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:31.111
There's no way you're going to find out

00:09:31.111 --> 00:09:33.183
whether that's true unless you do it.

00:09:33.183 --> 00:09:36.786
So no one can tell you either because

00:09:36.786 --> 00:09:38.537
just because it works for someone else,

00:09:38.537 --> 00:09:40.911
that's interesting and all that,

00:09:40.911 --> 00:09:42.496
but it's no proof that it'll work for you.

00:09:42.496 --> 00:09:44.972
You have to be all in in this game.

00:09:44.972 --> 00:09:47.338
There is no more
effective way of operating

00:09:47.338 --> 00:09:50.103
in the world than to
conceptualize the highest good

00:09:50.103 --> 00:09:53.452
that you can, and then
strive to attain it.

00:09:53.452 --> 00:09:57.619
There's no more practical
pathway to the kind of success

00:09:59.095 --> 00:10:03.174
that you could have if you
actually knew what success was.

00:10:03.174 --> 00:10:07.241
The world shifts itself around your aim.

00:10:07.241 --> 00:10:09.193
Because you are a
creature that has an aim.

00:10:09.193 --> 00:10:11.429
You have to have an aim
in order to do something.

00:10:11.429 --> 00:10:12.635
You're an aiming creature.

00:10:12.635 --> 00:10:15.723
You look at a point and
you move towards it.

00:10:15.723 --> 00:10:17.975
It's built right into it,
and so you have an aim.

00:10:17.975 --> 00:10:21.205
Let's say your aim is
the highest possible aim.

00:10:21.205 --> 00:10:24.697
Well then so that sets
up the world around you.

00:10:24.697 --> 00:10:26.538
It organizes all of your perceptions,

00:10:26.538 --> 00:10:28.923
it organizes what you
see, and you don't see it.

00:10:28.923 --> 00:10:32.006
It organizes your emotions
and your motivations.

00:10:32.006 --> 00:10:33.654
So you organize yourself around that aim,

00:10:33.654 --> 00:10:36.361
and then what happens is
the day manifests itself

00:10:36.361 --> 00:10:39.114
as a set of challenges and problems,

00:10:39.114 --> 00:10:42.004
and if you solve them
properly, then you stay

00:10:42.004 --> 00:10:44.638
on the pathway towards that
aim, and you can concentrate

00:10:44.638 --> 00:10:47.804
on the day, and so that way
you get to have your cake

00:10:47.804 --> 00:10:51.805
and eat it too because you
can point into the distance,

00:10:51.805 --> 00:10:55.638
the far distance, and
you can live in the day.

00:10:57.216 --> 00:10:59.968
And it seems to me that
that makes every moment

00:10:59.968 --> 00:11:02.193
of the day super charged with meaning.

00:11:02.193 --> 00:11:05.272
Because if everything that
you're doing every day

00:11:05.272 --> 00:11:07.681
is related to the highest
possible aim that you

00:11:07.681 --> 00:11:10.235
can conceptualize, well
that's the very definition

00:11:10.235 --> 00:11:12.857
of the meaning that would
sustain you in your life.

00:11:12.857 --> 00:11:14.413
- Thinking completely
different is the key.

00:11:14.413 --> 00:11:16.161
If everyone is competing on one level,

00:11:16.161 --> 00:11:18.075
you got to think at another.

00:11:18.075 --> 00:11:21.409
Like for instance, I always
wanted to get into television,

00:11:21.409 --> 00:11:24.272
but TV it was always so crowded.

00:11:24.272 --> 00:11:26.836
Everyone's trying to get
in on Friday night on NBC,

00:11:26.836 --> 00:11:28.891
so what do you do when everyone,

00:11:28.891 --> 00:11:29.885
I've always heard this advice.

00:11:29.885 --> 00:11:31.846
It made sense only recently.

00:11:31.846 --> 00:11:33.191
When everyone is doing the same thing,

00:11:33.191 --> 00:11:34.609
when everyone is competing
in the same realm,

00:11:34.609 --> 00:11:36.671
you have to think much bigger.

00:11:36.671 --> 00:11:38.375
There's a lot less competition up there.

00:11:38.375 --> 00:11:40.748
There's nobody up there actually.

00:11:40.748 --> 00:11:43.422
- Find the hole to fill
it, instead of trying to

00:11:43.422 --> 00:11:44.572
get into other people's territory.

00:11:44.572 --> 00:11:45.908
- Yeah, so like I can't get my show on TV,

00:11:45.908 --> 00:11:47.947
I know, I'll own a network.

00:11:47.947 --> 00:11:49.920
Then I can put on any show that I want.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.004
And how many other people
are going up for a network?

00:11:52.004 --> 00:11:53.453
You know how many other people
applied for that network?

00:11:53.453 --> 00:11:54.586
- How many?

00:11:54.586 --> 00:11:56.595
It was a lot, and then it wasn't a lot.

00:11:56.595 --> 00:11:59.592
100 people in the whole country.

00:11:59.592 --> 00:12:02.600
In the whole country, 100
people threw in an idea

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:05.079
for a network and showed a presentation.

00:12:05.079 --> 00:12:06.097
That's not a lot of people.

00:12:06.097 --> 00:12:06.930
- [Reporter] That isn't a lot of people

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:08.346
for how many people have ideas.

00:12:08.346 --> 00:12:10.130
- That's a lot less people
that's even in this room.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.448
So when you think about that, think about

00:12:12.448 --> 00:12:14.393
how can I show somebody,
how can I get someone's

00:12:14.393 --> 00:12:16.546
attention, everyone
else is at the festival,

00:12:16.546 --> 00:12:19.080
don't go to the festival,
think of something,

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:21.626
I mean go to the festival,
but think of something also,

00:12:21.626 --> 00:12:22.956
something else beyond that.

00:12:22.956 --> 00:12:24.442
Don't rely on the festival
because then you're

00:12:24.442 --> 00:12:25.475
just crossing your fingers.

00:12:25.475 --> 00:12:26.932
You got to hit it from other ways.

00:12:26.932 --> 00:12:28.433
And that promotes much bigger thinking.

00:12:28.433 --> 00:12:31.610
Always say aim high because if
you aim just at the festival,

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.471
you might hit it and you
might just hit lower.

00:12:34.471 --> 00:12:36.608
But if you aim really
high, you might just still

00:12:36.608 --> 00:12:39.412
hit the festival, but at
least now you got to a chance

00:12:39.412 --> 00:12:41.829
to hit there, there, or like.

00:12:42.815 --> 00:12:45.323
- By why some say the moon?

00:12:45.323 --> 00:12:48.225
Why choose this as our goal?

00:12:48.225 --> 00:12:52.581
And they may well ask, why
climb the highest mountain?

00:12:52.581 --> 00:12:55.414
Why 35 years ago fly the Atlantic?

00:12:56.615 --> 00:12:58.655
Why does Rice play Texas?

00:12:58.655 --> 00:13:01.444
We choose to go to the moon.

00:13:01.444 --> 00:13:03.795
We choose to go to the moon.

00:13:03.795 --> 00:13:06.045
(applause)

00:13:09.482 --> 00:13:12.733
We choose to go to the moon in this decade

00:13:12.733 --> 00:13:15.638
and do the other things,
not because they are easy

00:13:15.638 --> 00:13:17.939
but because they are hard.

00:13:17.939 --> 00:13:21.493
Because that goal will serve to organize

00:13:21.493 --> 00:13:25.388
and measure the best of
our energies and skills.

00:13:25.388 --> 00:13:29.311
Because that challenge is one
that we're willing to accept.

00:13:29.311 --> 00:13:32.174
One we are unwilling to postpone.

00:13:32.174 --> 00:13:35.434
And one we intend to
win, and the others too.

